    "title": "pandas.ExcelFile.sheet_names — pandas 3.1.0.dev0+1386.gcb2086a1a4 documentation",
    "status": 200,
    "markdown": "# pandas.ExcelFile.sheet_names#\n\n- property ExcelFile.sheet_names[source]#\n- Names of the sheets in the document. This is particularly useful for loading a specific sheet into a DataFrame when you do not know the sheet names beforehand. \n  - Returns:\n    - list of str\n    - List of sheet names in the document.\n See also \n  - `ExcelFile.parse`\n  - Parse a sheet into a DataFrame.\n  - `read_excel`\n  - Read an Excel file into a pandas DataFrame. If you know the sheet names, it may be easier to specify them directly to read_excel.\n Examples >>> file = pd.ExcelFile(\"myfile.xlsx\") >>> file.sheet_names [\"Sheet1\", \"Sheet2\"]",
